cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the code and the paper below."
title: "RNTME-NAE: reference implementation of a task-level evaluation protocol for black-box attacks on vehicular perception"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of the RNTME-NAE ensemble gradient attack together with a
  layered evaluation protocol that separates targets used to generate an adversarial
  perturbation from targets that never take part. Ships the GTSRB transfer benchmark
  (eight attack methods, five seeds), the consequence-weighted metrics SW-ASR and DMR
  with their 43x43 semantic weight matrix, an object-detection extension and a suite of
  input-level defences evaluated under BPDA adaptive attacks. The headline result is a
  negative one: on a target that shares no training pipeline with the surrogates, the
  eight methods fall inside a narrow band and no comparison survives correction.
